WEBVTT

NOTE Cops (1922) - Riah TV captions

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.800
Buster Keaton in "Cops"

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.200
Written and directed by
Buster Keaton and Eddie Cline

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:23.000
"Love laughs at
locksmiths." —Houdini

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.200
[music]

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:44.000
"I won't marry you until you
become a big business man."

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:28.500
"I've telephoned
for the expressman."

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:57.000
"I'm broke and
they threw me out."

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.750
"If I don't sell my furniture
my wife and babies will starve."

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:14.000
"I'll buy it and prove
I'm a good business man."

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.250
"Maybe he was arrested
for speeding."

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:09.250
Once a year the citizens of
every city know where they can
find a policeman.

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:04.750
"I'm pleased to meet the
daughter of our Mayor."

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:34.500
"Get some cops to
protect our policemen."

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:11.250
"Do you suppose anything
could've happened to our
furniture?"
